cff-version: 1.2.0
title: IconKit
message: >-
  If you use IconKit or build on its skeleton-to-six-weights method, a credit
  is appreciated.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Devesh
    family-names: Shirsath
    website: https://deveshshirsath.com
repository-code: https://github.com/Devesh-Shirsath/IconKit
url: https://github.com/Devesh-Shirsath/IconKit
abstract: >-
  IconKit is a Claude Code skill that designs new icons in the Phosphor Icons
  style from a description of a feature. The model draws one skeleton of
  centrelines; a dependency-free Python build strokes it at Phosphor's four
  widths, derives the fill and duotone weights, outlines everything to
  production SVG, checks it against rules measured from Phosphor's 1,512
  icons, and renders a preview beside real ones.
keywords:
  - claude-code
  - claude-skill
  - icons
  - icon-design
  - phosphor-icons
  - svg
  - design-system
  - design-automation
  - figma
license: MIT
